{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the check-runs list is fetched twice per tick; share one probe**

`headPlaceholders()` (line 2353) and `headOrphanedRunChecks()` (line 2364) each call `headCheckRunsSafe(effectiveRepoInfo, vHead0)` against the **same** REST endpoint back-to-back, and the run rollup is then refetched again at line 2390. This roughly doubles the GitHub API traffic for every `validate_pr` evaluation of every candidate PR on every SM tick, even when the head carries nothing pending.

Both underlying detectors (`placeholders()`, `orphanedRunChecks()`) are already pure functions that take a check-runs array — fetch once at the call site and pass the parsed list into both:

```javascript
var vCheckRuns = vHead0 ? headCheckRunsSafe(effectiveRepoInfo, vHead0) : null;
var vPh = vCheckRuns === null ? null
    : checkRunZombiesModule.placeholders(vCheckRuns, Date.now(), { ... });
var vOrphans = vCheckRuns === null ? null
    : checkRunZombiesModule.orphanedRunChecks(vCheckRuns, ..., Date.now(), { ... });
```

That also structurally eliminates the `vPh === null`-with-orphans edge case behind the line-2400 comment.
